[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 821,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 764,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127954,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 764,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Arteriovenous malformation (AVM) is a congenital vascular anomaly characterized by abnormal arteriovenous connections and high-flow arteriovenous shunting.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 822,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 765,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127955,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 765,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9123/0 Arteriovenous malformation</p>\r\n<p>9123/0 Deep-seated arteriovenous malformation</p>\r\n<p>9123/0 Cutaneous arteriovenous malformation</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 823,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 766,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127956,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 766,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LA90.3Y Other specified peripheral arteriovenous malformations</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 824,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 767,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127957,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 767,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> arteriovenous haemangioma; cirsoid aneurysm; acral arteriovenous tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 825,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 768,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127958,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 768,
        "headingText": "<p>Deep-seated arteriovenous malformation; cutaneous arteriovenous malformation</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-06-30T10:34:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 826,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 769,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127959,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 769,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AVM can involve the skin, subcutis, bone, and viscera and has a marked predilection for the head, neck, and limbs. Small, superficial vascular lesions with a predilection for the lips, perioral skin, nose, and eyelids of middle-aged to elderly men, traditionally called acral arteriovenous tumour, may not be true AVMs.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 827,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 770,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127960,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 770,
        "headingText": "<p>AVMs involving skin and deep soft tissue are characterized by a poorly defined bluish or red mass that may be pulsatile, with variably severe arteriovenous shunting, sometimes leading to local tissue necrosis, haemorrhage, or high-output heart failure. The superficial subtype is typically a small red or blue papule. Deep-seated and cutaneous clinical subtypes have been described {17582945; 23125071}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2025-07-01T12:28:15"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 828,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 771,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127961,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 771,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>AVMs have no sex predilection. They are congenital but may not become clinically evident until later in life. Most are solitary and sporadic.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 829,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 772,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127962,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 772,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases are sporadic. Inherited lesions occurring as part of the rare capillary malformation&ndash;AVM syndrome are associated with germline <em>RASA1</em> mutations, which are probably causative {20007727}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 830,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 773,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127963,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 773,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 837,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 780,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127964,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 780,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>See <em>Clinical features</em>, above.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 831,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 774,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127965,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 774,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The lesions are histologically heterogeneous but primarily show beds of arterioles, capillaries, and venules set within a fibromyxomatous background, intermixed with larger-calibre arteries and thick-walled veins. In lesions with high-grade shunting, the arteries are tortuous, with fragmented mural elastic laminae, and the veins show irregular intima and/or mural fibrosis, reflective of elevated venous pressure and turbulence. The overlying skin often contains a small-vessel proliferation similar to that seen in ischaemia and stasis. Superficial scalp AVMs, which are limited in depth by cranial bone, are histologically similar.</p>\r\n<h6>Differential diagnosis</h6>\r\n<p>Diagnosis typically requires careful clinicopathological correlation and radiological studies, particularly in small samples. Focal cellular small-vessel proliferations in AVM can mimic infantile haemangioma but are GLUT1-negative {28552538}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 832,
    "bookid": 64,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 775,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 127966,
        "bookId": 64,
        "chapterId": 260,
        "headingId": 775,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2025-04-25T12:04:55"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
